Source: perfcached
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Yury Kirsanov <yury@kfi.net.au>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               libsodium-dev,
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: perfcached
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Conflicts: perfcached-standalone
Replaces: perfcached-standalone
Description: in-memory cache daemon with a durable write-ahead log
 perfcached is a clustered in-memory cache and store: a lock-free read
 path, a write-ahead log with real crash recovery, and periodic
 snapshots.  It speaks its own binary protocol plus a
 RESP-compatible surface, so existing Redis clients can talk to it
 without changes.
 .
 Cluster modes are a property of the cluster, not of a node: store
 (every node holds everything), proxy (placed single-copy) and shard
 (ownership computed by rendezvous hashing).
 .
 Read PRODUCTION.md before a first deployment: the durability knobs
 depend on what the storage actually measures, and the daemon reports
 that at startup.

Package: perfcached-standalone
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Conflicts: perfcached
Replaces: perfcached
Provides: perfcached
Description: in-memory cache daemon with a durable write-ahead log (single node)
 The standalone edition of perfcached, for a cache that will only ever
 be one node: the same daemon, protocols, write-ahead log, snapshots,
 RESP-compatible surface, tools (perfcli, perfdump, perfload) and client
 library as the perfcached package, built without the cluster code.  The
 binary is about a third smaller and its static memory smaller, and a
 [cluster] section in the configuration is refused rather than ignored.
 .
 It installs the same files as the perfcached package, under the same
 names, so the two replace each other.
 .
 Read PRODUCTION.md before a first deployment: the durability knobs
 depend on what the storage actually measures, and the daemon reports
 that at startup.
